      "dx_date_max": null
    },
    "text": "Bilateral or contralateral nodes are classified as regional nodes for head, neck, and truncal tumors with bidirectional drainage to primary nodal basins, as shown on lymphoscintigraphy.\n\nTruncal tumors may also drain to both cephalad and caudal primary nodal basins as shown on lymphoscintigraphy.\n\nClinical assessment of bilateral/contralateral or cephalad/caudal regional nodal involvement is required for tumors where lymphoscintigraphy is not performed",
    "codes": null,
    "notes": null
  },
  {
